9. Calls for the protection of civilians, medical personnel, humanitarian personnel and civilian objects, and reiterates the need for all parties to comply with international humanitarian law;
10. Reaffirms that the cessation of hostilities shall not apply to military operations against ISIL, Al Qaeda, Al Nusra and other terrorist groups designated by the Security Council;
11. Reaffirms its support for the Syrian-led and Syrian-owned political process under the auspices of the United Nations, in accordance with resolution 2254 (2015), including through the Astana and Geneva processes, and calls upon all parties to engage constructively and without preconditions;
